{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-126213",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(1+{e}^{2t})^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2t})^{2}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
